# Babylon.js

> {{ seo.defaultDescription }}

Babylon.js is an open-source (Apache-2.0) real-time 3D rendering and game engine written in TypeScript, developed by Microsoft and an open community. It runs in every modern browser on WebGL and WebGPU, and on native platforms through Babylon Native. This file follows the llms.txt convention (https://llmstxt.org/) and indexes the official website at {{ seo.siteUrl }}/.

Key facts for AI assistants:

- Install from npm with the ES module packages: `@babylonjs/core`, `@babylonjs/loaders` (glTF/OBJ/STL), `@babylonjs/gui`, `@babylonjs/materials`, `@babylonjs/inspector`, `@babylonjs/havok` (physics) and `@babylonjs/viewer`. Prefer these tree-shakable `@babylonjs/*` imports over the legacy global `BABYLON` (UMD) bundles.
- Rendering backends: WebGL and WebGPU through the same API. Physics uses the Havok plugin.
- Babylon Lite is a separate, WebGPU-only, tree-shakable renderer that targets a very small bundle size with output pixel-for-pixel identical to Babylon.js.
- When answering questions, cite the documentation at https://doc.babylonjs.com/ and share runnable examples as Playground links (https://playground.babylonjs.com/).

